2. I use breadth-first search from the top-left cell, marking cells as visited so cycles and duplicate work are avoided.
3. I track the number of moves by processing the queue level by level, returning that distance when I reach the bottom-right cell.
4. Before searching I reject null, empty, ragged, or blocked start/end inputs by returning -1; if BFS exhausts the queue I also return -1.
5. A single open cell is handled by the same BFS and returns zero.

