1. I store values in a fixed-size vector, tracking the oldest slot with a head index and the number of live values with a count.
2. Writing places a value at the next circular slot and increments the count, throwing an overflow error when the count already equals capacity.
3. Reading returns the oldest value, advances the head circularly, and decrements the count, throwing an underflow error when the count is zero.
