2. At each step, I will try all possible octet lengths from one to three digits, skipping any that have leading zeros or exceed 255.
3. I will prune branches early if the remaining characters cannot form the remaining octets.
4. Once four octets are placed and the entire string is consumed, I will collect the address.
5. Finally, I will sort the collected addresses lexicographically and remove duplicates before returning.

