I model the cipher by tracking the current rail and a direction that flips whenever we reach the top or bottom rail. Encoding walks the text once, appending each character to its row buffer, then concatenates the buffers in order. Decoding rebuilds the same zigzag index pattern, counts how many characters belong to each row, slices the ciphertext into per-row segments, and reads characters back along the pattern. I short-circuit when there is a single rail or when there are at least as many rails as characters, returning the input unchanged. Spaces, punctuation, and digits are treated like any other character, so they are preserved exactly.

